From 000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Devoogdt <thomas@devoogdt.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] backend-drm: avoid __VA_OPT__ in debug macro

__VA_OPT__ is only available with recent C preprocessors and is not
understood by the old compilers supported by Buildroot. Use the traditional
GNU ## token pasting extension already relied on throughout Weston instead.

Upstream: pending
Signed-off-by: Thomas Devoogdt <thomas@devoogdt.com>
---
 libweston/backend-drm/drm-internal.h | 9 +--------
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libweston/backend-drm/drm-internal.h b/libweston/backend-drm/drm-internal.h
index 829a1f4..f5ceb7b 100644
--- a/libweston/backend-drm/drm-internal.h
+++ b/libweston/backend-drm/drm-internal.h
@@ -122,9 +122,2 @@
-#define DO_DRM_DEBUG_COMPLEX(scope, ...) \
-	weston_log_scope_printf(scope, __VA_ARGS__)
-
-#define DO_DRM_DEBUG(scope, string) \
-	weston_log_scope_puts(scope, string)
-
-#define drm_debug(b, format, ...)				\
-	DO_DRM_DEBUG ## __VA_OPT__(_COMPLEX)			\
-	((b)->debug, format __VA_OPT__(,) __VA_ARGS__)
+#define drm_debug(b, format, ...) \
+	weston_log_scope_printf((b)->debug, format, ##__VA_ARGS__)
